{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>That you may remember and do all My commandments.</b> The section of tzitzit is juxtaposed to the section of the wood-gatherer, because when the wood-gatherer was judged for desecrating Shabbat, Israel said: how can we ensure observance of Shabbat — today or tomorrow we may be liable to such a death? For on a festival there is a recognizable sign in its observance, but not so with Shabbat. Therefore He gave them the commandment of tzitzit to engage with on Shabbat, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said: whoever walks on Shabbat without tzitzit is as if he gathers wood on Shabbat." "<b>And you shall be holy to your Elohim.</b> And who is your Elohim?"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:10.285576192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}